      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackson%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city was renamed in 1822 to honor General Andrew Jackson, a War of 1812 hero.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackson%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Jackson grew into a railroad hub, serving as a junction for north–south, east–west, and west–east lines between Memphis and Nashville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackson%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1831, Micajah Autry, the Alamo hero, practiced law in Jackson before returning to Texas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
